      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Of which: 100 koku — the exempt land of Hikozaemon, a peasant of Sanbongi village in Echigo Province. The attached note states that the domain will report this parcel's revenue only after investigating it, i.e. the yield was not yet ascertained at the time of the survey. The 内 marker heading the whole three-item breakdown prints at the top of this column; the note is a warichu (double-column) note too long for one line and wraps to the line at left (right line 越後國三本木村百姓彦左衛門, 13 glyphs; left line 除地歳入取調之上可申上候, 12 glyphs)."
      },
